function ReleaseV04() { return <><article className="release-v04"><span>v0.4.3 · Unified Experience</span><h2>One platform, user-controlled depth</h2><ul><li>Removed the global Learning and Bench mode switch.</li><li>Unified AST Compass into one scientific experience.</li><li>Added progressive disclosure for deeper educational explanations.</li><li>Simplified navigation and mobile layout.</li><li>Preserved Learn, AST Detective, BCID, Concordance, account architecture, and scientific results.</li></ul></article><article className="release-v04"><span>v0.4.2 · Product Clarity &amp; Trust Update</span><h2>Clearer workflows, stronger trust signals</h2><ul><li>Simplified the homepage around three primary workflows.</li><li>Elevated BCID Forecast and Concordance as signature features.</li><li>Added a dedicated Resistance hub and cleaned Learn routing.</li><li>Added an evidence-aware scientific content-status framework without unsupported review claims.</li><li>Improved grouped global search, mobile navigation, and product clarity.</li><li>Standardized astcompass.com as the canonical production domain with SEO metadata and redirects.</li></ul></article><article className="release-v04"><span>v0.4.1 · Sep 1, 2026</span><h2>Lookup, Image Concordance &amp; BCID Upgrade</h2><ul><li>Rebuilt BCID Forecast around the complete manufacturer panel menu: 26 bacterial, 7 yeast, and all 10 AMR targets.</li><li>Added bidirectional, many-to-many organism–marker filtering, multiplex attribution matrices, and conservative combined forecasts.</li><li>Added full account-free scientific access.</li><li>Prepared provider-backed account, dashboard, history, image-workspace, and settings architecture with deny-by-default database policies for future validation.</li><li>Added an automated pre-preview PHI screening gate that blocks suspected identifiers and fails closed without an override.</li><li>Public image work remains session-only; permanent private-image saving stays disabled until the reviewed backend and second-stage scanner are configured.</li><li>Alphabetized long lookup lists and added reusable alias-aware search controls.</li></ul><h3>v0.4.0 · Breakpoint &amp; BCID foundation</h3><ul><li>Expanded breakpoint architecture for bacteria, fungi, Rapid AST, no-breakpoint, and ECOFF states.</li><li>Added species-aware BCID overrides, antimicrobial-class grouping, and marker limitations.</li><li>Breakpoint values remain educational demo data—not for clinical interpretation.</li></ul></article></>; }

